section: quotas
title: Quotas and limits
about: |
  The quotas of the cloud and the floors of Palette: what a build asks for, against what the
  account can give.
rules:
- id: aws-quotas
  title: The vCPU quota of the region covers the pools
  engines:
  - aws
  - eks
  tier: cloud
  severity: fail
  status: source
  what: |
    A build asks EC2 for the vCPUs of each pool, one VPC, one internet gateway, and a load
    balancer. Each zone adds an elastic IP and a NAT gateway. A quota that is short fails during
    the build with `VcpuLimitExceeded`, `VpcLimitExceeded`, `AddressLimitExceeded`, or
    `NatGatewayLimitExceeded`. Palette reads no quota. The check reads one quota, the on-demand
    standard vCPUs (`L-1216C47A`), and compares its value with the vCPUs the on-demand pools ask
    for. It counts 4 vCPUs for an `xlarge` type, 4 for each multiple (`2xlarge` is 8), and 2 for a
    smaller size. The vCPU count of a type is not in the entity. The check does not read the
    usage, so a pass is not a proof. The other quotas are in the reproduce lines.
  check:
    kind: exec
    needs:
    - aws
    argv:
    - aws
    - service-quotas
    - get-service-quota
    - --service-code
    - ec2
    - --quota-code
    - L-1216C47A
    - --region
    - '{{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }}'
    - --output
    - json
    expr: |
      def vcpus: (split(".") | .[1] // "") as $s
        | if $s == "xlarge" then 4
          elif ($s | test("^[0-9]+xlarge$")) then ($s | rtrimstr("xlarge") | tonumber) * 4
          else 2 end;
      .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region as $r
      | ([ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[]
           | select((.cloudConfig.capacityType // "on-demand") != "spot")
           | select((.poolConfig.size // 0) > 0)
           | { name: .poolConfig.name, size: .poolConfig.size, type: (.cloudConfig.instanceType // ""), v: ((.cloudConfig.instanceType // "") | vcpus) } ]) as $pools
      | ([ $pools[] | .size * .v ] | add // 0) as $need
      | if .exec.exit != 0 then ["aws service-quotas get-service-quota failed: \(.exec.stderr | .[:200])"]
        else (.exec.stdout.Quota.Value // 0) as $q
        | if $q < $need
          then ["the on-demand vCPU quota L-1216C47A in \($r) is \($q), and the pools ask for \($need) vCPUs: \([ $pools[] | "\(.size) x \(.type)" ] | join(", "))"]
          else [] end
        end
  reproduce:
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code ec2 --quota-code L-1216C47A --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value   # on-demand standard vCPUs; L-34B43A08 is the spot vCPUs; L-0263D0A3 is the elastic IPs'
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code vpc --quota-code L-F678F1CE --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value   # VPCs for each region; L-A4707A72 internet gateways; L-FE5A380F NAT gateways for each zone'
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code elasticloadbalancing --quota-code L-E9E9831D --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value   # application load balancers; L-69A177A2 network load balancers'
  - 'aws ec2 describe-vpcs --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query ''length(Vpcs)''; aws ec2 describe-addresses --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query ''length(Addresses)''; aws ec2 describe-nat-gateways --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query ''length(NatGateways)''   # the usage'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: A preflight route that reads the quotas and the usage, and reports "unknown" without the permission.
  evidence:
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-resource-limits.html
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/amazon-vpc-limits.html
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/aws/vcpu-quota-low.json
    clean: fixtures/aws/vcpu-quota-clean.json
- id: eks-quotas
  title: The EKS quotas cover the cluster and its node groups
  engines:
  - eks
  tier: cloud
  severity: fail
  status: source
  what: |
    EKS limits the clusters in a region (`L-1194D53C`, 100 by default). It limits the managed node
    groups of a cluster (`L-6D54EA21`, 30), and the nodes of a node group (`L-BD136A63`, 450). A
    build over a limit fails with `ResourceLimitExceeded`. The check reads the nodes for each node group
    and compares the value with the size and the maximum size of each worker pool. The clusters in
    the region need the usage too; that line is in the reproduce lines.
  check:
    kind: exec
    needs:
    - aws
    argv:
    - aws
    - service-quotas
    - get-service-quota
    - --service-code
    - eks
    - --quota-code
    - L-BD136A63
    - --region
    - '{{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }}'
    - --output
    - json
    expr: |
      .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region as $r
      | if .exec.exit != 0 then ["aws service-quotas get-service-quota failed: \(.exec.stderr | .[:200])"]
        else (.exec.stdout.Quota.Value // 0) as $q
        | [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[]
            | select((.poolConfig.isControlPlane // false) | not)
            | (if (.poolConfig.maxSize // 0) > (.poolConfig.size // 0) then .poolConfig.maxSize else (.poolConfig.size // 0) end) as $n
            | select($n > $q)
            | "pool \(.poolConfig.name) asks for \($n) nodes, and the quota L-BD136A63 (nodes for each managed node group) in \($r) is \($q)" ]
        end
  reproduce:
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code eks --quota-code L-1194D53C --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value; aws eks list-clusters --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query ''length(clusters)''   # clusters for each region, and the usage'
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code eks --quota-code L-6D54EA21 --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value   # managed node groups for each cluster; the entity has {{ [ .entity.spec.machinepoolconfig[] | select((.poolConfig.isControlPlane // false) | not) ] | length }} worker pool(s)'
  - 'aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code eks --quota-code L-BD136A63 --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value   # nodes for each managed node group'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: A preflight route that reads the quotas and the usage, and reports "unknown" without the permission.
  evidence:
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/service-quotas.html
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/node-quota-low.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/node-quota-clean.json
- id: aws-sg-rules
  title: The rules of a security group stay under the quota
  engines:
  - aws
  tier: cloud
  severity: warn
  status: inferred
  what: |
    CAPA writes the rules of the node security group, and the CNI and the load balancers add more.
    The quota `L-E79EC296` (inbound or outbound rules for each security group, 60 by default) can
    run out during the build or later, with `RulesPerSecurityGroupLimitExceeded`. No security group
    exists before the build, so a check needs the groups of a cluster that runs: the reproduce lines
    read them. This is a reading of the source, not a run.
  reproduce:
  - aws service-quotas get-service-quota --service-code vpc --quota-code L-E79EC296 --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --query Quota.Value
  - 'aws ec2 describe-security-groups --region {{ .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region }} --filters Name=tag-key,Values=sigs.k8s.io/cluster-api-provider-aws/role --query ''SecurityGroups[].[GroupId,GroupName,length(IpPermissions),length(IpPermissionsEgress)]'' --output table   # the groups CAPA made, during or after the build'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Report the quota and the count of rules in a preflight route, with "unknown" without the permission.
  evidence:
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/amazon-vpc-limits.html#vpc-limits-security-groups
